            name: "batch-get-deployment-targets",
            description: Some("Returns an array of one or more targets associated with a deployment. This method works with all compute types and should be used instead of the deprecated BatchGetDeploymentInstances. The maximum number of targets that can be returned is 25.  The type of targets returned depends on the deployment's compute platform or deployment method:     EC2/On-premises: Information about Amazon EC2 instance targets.     Lambda: Information about Lambda functions targets.     Amazon ECS: Information about Amazon ECS service targets.     CloudFormation: Information about targets of blue/green deployments initiated by a CloudFormation stack update"),
            options: [
